        "species": 39,
        "text": "For most jumping spiders, nobody has measured how sharply you see. If you are a Phidippus johnsoni, your big front eyes see about an eighth of the detail a human sees, and you very likely share that with other Phidippus spiders. If you are a bold jumping spider, the light-sensing cells in the sharpest zone of each of your side eyes sit about half a degree apart.",
