        "species": 39,
        "text": "If you are a bold jumping spider, each of the eyes just beside your two big front eyes sees about 70 degrees from side to side and about 100 degrees from top to bottom. The only other measurement is a side-to-side span of about 100 degrees for those eyes in Menemerus semilimbatus, a gray wall jumping spider's relative. Nobody has measured the rest, including how far the fields of your two eyes overlap.",
