          "g": 0.0,
          "i": 1.0
        },
        "species": 39,
        "text": "Inside each of your two big front eyes, the retina moves, scanning across what you look at. If you are a bold jumping spider, your front eyes scan a still shape the same way with or without the eyes beside them, but they rely on those eyes to find and track a moving one. Nobody has measured this in most other jumping spiders, so nobody knows how closely you match the bold jumping spider.",
