        "text": "When something moves near you, you turn to face it. If you are a bold jumping spider, your big front eyes scan differently when dots move like a living animal than when they move in other ways. If you are a magnolia green jumping spider, the retinas of your side eyes are less refined for sensing motion than those of the other jumping spiders studied, and for most species nobody has measured how well you see movement.",
