        "text": "If you are a bold jumping spider, a low tone in the air makes you freeze, even when it comes from more than 3 meters away, and a shaking surface under your feet is unpleasant enough that you learn to avoid whatever you were looking at. If you are a brilliant jumping spider, the rate of a courting male's vibrations is an important part of whether he wins a mate. Nobody has measured what most other jumping spiders sense of sound or vibration.",
